Package: fresh-editor
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, libc6 (>= 2.30), libgcc-s1 (>= 4.2)
Description: terminal IDE and text editor with LSP and TypeScript plugins
 Fresh is a fast, lightweight terminal-based IDE and text editor that aims to
 be easy to pick up: familiar keybindings, mouse support, a command palette
 and menus, with no modal editing required.
 .
 It provides syntax highlighting, multi-cursor editing, LSP integration
 (completion, diagnostics, go to definition), a file explorer, split panes,
 integrated terminals, and a TypeScript plugin runtime. Large files open
 instantly. A session daemon keeps the editor running in the background so a
 terminal can re-attach later (fresh -a), and fresh --web serves the same
 editor to a browser.
 .
 The command is "fresh". This package repackages the upstream Debian build,
 including its man page, desktop entry and icons; updates are delivered by
 apt, and the built-in updater defers to it.
